Z||000004||JBGehling||02-11-2001||08:34 AM||||I mean, does the decal run exactly parallel to the red stripe on the bottom or is it at a minor diagonal angle... does the decal sit ON the red stripe, or slightly above it?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||02-11-2001||11:54 AM||||Since all the decals were add ons during the manufacture of the car or during dealer installation, each decal position will probably be slightly different. I think you could buy the Pace car without the decals and the dealer would do the install.  To me it looks like the OFFICIAL PACE CAR decal runs parallel to the red stripe and above it.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 02-11-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||Songman||02-11-2001||01:41 PM||||As has been mentioned, the placement was actually done by the dealer or the person that bought the car.<P>In the two photos above you can see that on the 'real' pace car the decals are parallel with the red stripe, while on the 'street' pace car the stripes are parallel with the black molding.<P>Do it according to which one you think looks best.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
